# Command Creation & Management Guidelines

> **PRIORITY**: HIGHEST - Essential for maintaining command system integrity and AI agent performance

## **QUICK REFERENCE**

- Target 80-130 lines (sweet spot: ~100 lines) for optimal AI processing
- Use consistent structure: Metadata → Purpose → Usage → Parameters → What It Does → Workflow → Integration → Related Commands
- Focus on "how to use" - commands describe usage, rules contain validation criteria
- Never auto-apply fixes - always require explicit flags and user confirmation
- Never generate summary/md files - only report findings unless explicitly requested
- Universal design - commands work on any project type, any language

## **CORE PRINCIPLES**

### **OPTIMAL AI PERFORMANCE**

- Target 80-130 lines total for maximum AI comprehension
- Use consistent structure across all commands for predictable processing
- Focus on actionable usage guidance over detailed validation criteria
- Maintain logical flow from purpose → usage → parameters → integration

### **CONSISTENCY & MAINTAINABILITY**

- All commands follow the same template for predictable AI processing
- Consistent section order: Metadata → Purpose → Usage → Parameters → What It Does → Workflow → Integration → Related Commands
- Uniform formatting (tables, code blocks, emphasis) across all commands
- Clear distinction between commands (how to use) and rules (what to check)

### **UNIVERSAL DESIGN**

- Commands must work on any project type (Python, JavaScript, Go, etc.)
- Language-agnostic where possible, framework-agnostic examples
- Minimal dependencies (only `.cursor/rules/00-*.mdc` files)
- 100% portable - copy to any project without modification

